    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>f(9)=2.9</m>:
at 9 AM, 2.9 centimeters of rain have fallen.




<alert>(b)</alert>
<m>f^{-1}(7)=10</m>:
7 centimeters of rain have fallen 10 hours after midnight.




<alert>(c)</alert>
<m>f'(9)=0.4</m>:
at 9 AM, the rain is falling at a rate of 0.4 cm/hr, so approximately 0.0067 cm of rain falls between 9 AM and 9:01 AM.




<alert>(d)</alert>
<m>(f^{-1})'(7)=3</m>:
when 7 centimeters of rain have fallen, it is accumulating at a rate of 1/3 cm/hr, so it takes approximately 18 min for the total accumulation to go from 7 to 7.1 cm .




</solution>
